  "id": "DrugBank_DB11737 - MONDO_8903",
  "verbalization": "Icotinib is associated with Lung Cancer through a chain of indications that link it to non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC), a primary disease entity. The evidence suggests that Icotinib is used to treat NSCLC, which in turn is indicated for treatment of Lung Cancer. This creates a circular relationship where Icotinib is linked to NSCLC, which is then linked to Lung Cancer, forming a closed loop of indications. The presence of multiple pathways, each connecting Icotinib to a different agent (Pembrolizumab, Nivolumab, and Pemetrexed) that are all indicated for Lung Cancer, supports the notion that Icotinib may be repurposed for Lung Cancer. The integration of these indications highlights the potential for Icotinib to be used in the treatment of Lung Cancer, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The evidence suggests a possible dependency on immune checkpoint inhibitors or chemotherapy agents, but the precise relationship remains to be elucidated.",
